# =============================================================================
# Credential template — PLACEHOLDERS ONLY. Never put a real key in this file.
#
#     cp .env.example .env      # then edit .env, which is git-ignored
#
# Everything here is OPTIONAL. With no keys at all this package still runs:
# QC, doublet detection, HVG, PCA/UMAP, Leiden, the CellTypist voter, cluster and
# cell-type markers, donor-level pseudobulk DESeq2, composition, and the report
# skeleton. What needs credentials is listed against each variable.
#
# It also runs with no NETWORK: all 41 CellTypist models ship in
# shared_reference/celltypist_models/. See the CellTypist section at the bottom.
# =============================================================================

# --- LLM access (OpenRouter, OpenAI-compatible) -------------------------------
# Needed for: the knowledge-based annotation voter, the PubMed voter's
# adjudication step, automatic tissue / CellTypist-model / SingleR-reference /
# DPT-root selection, and the report's narrative sections.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_KEY
LLM_MODEL_FAST=anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.6

# The consensus annotator (celltype_consensus/config.py) reads OPENROUTER_MODEL
# specifically. Mirror LLM_MODEL_FAST here or the LLM voter stays off.
OPENROUTER_MODEL=anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.6

# Optional LLM tuning (defaults shown)
# LLM_MAX_RETRIES=3
# LLM_TIMEOUT_S=60
# LLM_TEMPERATURE=0

# --- LLM provider selector ----------------------------------------------------
# Values: openrouter | openai | anthropic
# NOTE: not yet wired in code — the pipeline always uses OpenRouter today. This
# takes effect only once the client layer reads it.
LLM_PROVIDER=openrouter

# --- PubMed literature voter (NCBI E-utilities) --------------------------------
# Optional. Without a key the client throttles to 3 requests/s; with one it goes
# to 10 requests/s. NCBI asks that automated clients identify themselves.
NCBI_API_KEY=REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_NCBI_KEY
NCBI_EMAIL=you@example.org

# --- Static reference data ----------------------------------------------------
# Root that CONTAINS the reference buckets shipped in ./shared_reference/.
# Leave as-is for this standalone package; repoint if the datasets live elsewhere.
SHARED_REFERENCE_ROOT=shared_reference

# --- SingleR / R --------------------------------------------------------------
# Only needed when the SingleR voter is enabled AND Rscript is not on PATH.
# Requires R >= 4.x with SingleR, celldex, SummarizedExperiment, Matrix, scrapper.
# R_HOME=C:\Program Files\R\R-4.5.1

# --- Voter overrides — REAL ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES ONLY, NOT THIS FILE ---------
# These two are read by pipeline.py BEFORE .env is loaded (the load happens inside
# the consensus config, which is built later in the run), so setting them here has
# NO EFFECT. Verified 2026-08-05 by tracing when the file becomes visible.
# Export them in the shell instead, or set the matching config.yaml keys:
#     PowerShell:  $env:CONSENSUS_ENABLE_SINGLER = '1'
#     bash:        export CONSENSUS_ENABLE_PUBMED=0
# CONSENSUS_ENABLE_SINGLER   1/true/yes enables SingleR when config says null
# CONSENSUS_ENABLE_PUBMED    0/false/no force-disables the PubMed voter
#
# Everything ELSE in this file works, because it is read after the load:
# OPENROUTER_*, LLM_*, NCBI_*, SHARED_REFERENCE_ROOT, R_HOME, CELLTYPIST_FOLDER.

# --- CellTypist models --------------------------------------------------------
# Not needed. All 41 models the pipeline can select are bundled at
#     shared_reference/celltypist_models/data/models/*.pkl        (53.3 MB)
# and are found automatically, so a first run needs no download. Set this ONLY to
# override that — e.g. to share one cache across several checkouts, or to point at
# a newer model set. The folder must use CellTypist's own <root>/data/models
# layout; the bundle already does, so the bundle itself is a valid value.
# CELLTYPIST_FOLDER=C:\path\to\celltypist_root
#
# Verify the bundle:  python tests/test_celltypist_offline.py
# Checksums:          shared_reference/celltypist_models/data/models/SHA256SUMS.txt
